# HTTP Strict Transport Security.
#
# Copy this file to 'hsts.caddy' in the same directory, and restart
# Caddy, ONCE THE DOMAIN IS SETTLED AND NOT BEFORE (plan section 3).
#
# What "settled" means: the name will not change, every service on it
# will be reachable over HTTPS for at least the max-age below, and the
# certificate will keep being one the browser accepts.  A browser that
# has seen this header refuses plain HTTP to this name until the
# max-age expires, and there is no way to tell it to stop sooner.
#
# Two years, which is what a preload list asks for.  'includeSubDomains'
# covers names that do not exist yet, so leave it off until every
# subdomain of this name is served over HTTPS as well.
header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=63072000"
